STYLE="Semi-realistic painterly guofeng portrait style, near-3D realistic rendering with fine detail, matching image 2 for drawing style, skin and fabric rendering (image 2 is a style reference only, never its face or body). Full-body standing figure head to feet, centered. "
TAIL=" A poised woman of about 36, mature graceful beauty, clearly older than a young girl, luminous fair skin. Eyes open and lively, 3/4 pose, brighter pleasant closed-lip smile (lips closed, no teeth), clean bare forehead with no mark. All flowers are fine silk-thread embroidery stitched directly into the fabric, flat, real hand embroidery lying in the weave and folds, not appliqué, not pasted patches, not raised. Clean transparent background, no glow, no haze."
NOPH=" NO phoenix and no long-tailed bird anywhere on the robe: replace every phoenix with peonies, flowers and butterflies."
YEL=" Image 3 is a COLOUR reference only (never its figure): the yellow, the other robe colours and the crown/hairpin gold exactly in the tones of the colour reference image (fresh royal yellow, lighter depth, 18K gold), not pale cream, not beige/tan/ochre, not heavy mustard, not lemon."
def recolour(orig,col,item,extra=""):
    return STYLE+f"Image 1 is the figure to copy: copy EXACTLY the face, hair shape, costume cut and layers, pose, fabric material and stitching layout and the one held {item}. Change the robe colour to a soft muted {col} (elegant, low saturation, completely different from the original {orig}). New hair ornaments, different from image 1 but based on its set and similar in style, size and richness, with gems matching the {col} robe. The {item} in a contrasting colour, not the robe colour, kept below the chin, the whole face fully visible."+NOPH+extra+TAIL
def t7(mode,orig,col,item,old):
    # mode v0: keep colour; v1/v2: recolour main, C2 yellow parts only
    base=STYLE+"Image 1 is the figure to copy: copy EXACTLY the phoenix crown and hairpins, face, costume cut and layers, pose, fabric material and stitching"
    itm=f" and the held item replaced by ONE {item} (in a contrasting colour, not the robe colour, kept below the chin, the whole face fully visible, hand really gripping it; no {old})"
    if mode=="v0":
        return base+f", every colour (EXACT colours of image 1: {orig}, NOT changed)"+itm+", redrawn at 2K on a transparent background. A clear embroidered phoenix as the main stitched motif on the robe, with flowers."+YEL+TAIL
    return base+itm+f". Change the MAIN robe colour to a soft muted {col} (elegant, low saturation, completely different from the original {orig}); the yellow only on parts (borders, sash, collar edge, a narrow inner panel), NEVER a wide yellow inner robe filling the front. Keep the phoenix crown of image 1 (same crown design and size), only vary small ornaments and gem colours. A clear embroidered phoenix as the main stitched motif on the robe, with flowers."+YEL+TAIL
